  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Find the area and perimeter of a rectangle with:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-q15-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "length $2\\sqrt{3}$ and width $4\\sqrt{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Area: $8\\sqrt{6}$ square units; perimeter: $4\\sqrt{3}+8\\sqrt{2}$ units.",
          "worked": "Using $A=lw$ and $P=2(l+w)$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=(2\\sqrt{3})(4\\sqrt{2})\\\\A&=8\\sqrt{6}\\text{ square units}\\\\P&=2(2\\sqrt{3}+4\\sqrt{2})\\\\P&=4\\sqrt{3}+8\\sqrt{2}\\text{ units}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q15-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "length $2\\sqrt{3}$ and width $4\\sqrt{3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Area: $24$ square units; perimeter: $12\\sqrt{3}$ units.",
          "worked": "Using $A=lw$ and $P=2(l+w)$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=(2\\sqrt{3})(4\\sqrt{3})\\\\A&=8\\times3\\\\A&=24\\text{ square units}\\\\P&=2(2\\sqrt{3}+4\\sqrt{3})\\\\P&=2(6\\sqrt{3})\\\\P&=12\\sqrt{3}\\text{ units}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q15-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "length $7+2\\sqrt{5}$ and width $7-2\\sqrt{5}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Area: $29$ square units; perimeter: $28$ units.\n\nExpand the product for the area; the surd terms cancel when adding adjacent sides.",
          "worked": "Using $A=lw$ and $P=2(l+w)$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=(7+2\\sqrt{5})(7-2\\sqrt{5})\\\\A&=49-14\\sqrt{5}+14\\sqrt{5}-4\\times5\\\\A&=49-20\\\\A&=29\\text{ square units}\\\\P&=2\\bigl((7+2\\sqrt{5})+(7-2\\sqrt{5})\\bigr)\\\\P&=2\\times14\\\\P&=28\\text{ units}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q15-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "length $1+\\sqrt{5}$ and width $2+\\sqrt{5}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Area: $7+3\\sqrt{5}$ square units; perimeter: $6+4\\sqrt{5}$ units.\n\nExpand the product for the area and collect like surds.",
          "worked": "Using $A=lw$ and $P=2(l+w)$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=(1+\\sqrt{5})(2+\\sqrt{5})\\\\A&=2+\\sqrt{5}+2\\sqrt{5}+5\\\\A&=7+3\\sqrt{5}\\text{ square units}\\\\P&=2\\bigl((1+\\sqrt{5})+(2+\\sqrt{5})\\bigr)\\\\P&=2(3+2\\sqrt{5})\\\\P&=6+4\\sqrt{5}\\text{ units}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
  },
